'''Masayoshi Kido''' was defeated in the [[Okaiken general election, 2026|2026 general election]], losing his [[Kochi Prefecture|Kochi]] 2nd constituency to [[Kumagai Natsuki]] (SCP).
'''Shinobu Andō''' was the longest-serving Defense Minister of the 21st century, serving throughout the entirety of the Honda premiership until the 2025 coalition reshuffle. Andō oversaw the initial integration of Satori AI into military operations and the adoption of the Industrial Sovereignty doctrine.
'''Toshio Hagiwara''' served across two administrations, having been appointed by SCP Prime Minister Aoyagi and retained by PPO Prime Minister Honda—a rare instance of cross-party continuity in a senior defense portfolio.
'''Naoko Shimazu''' was the first woman to serve as Defense Minister, appointed during the Aoyagi administration following the Thirteenth Amendment. Her tenure was marked by the establishment of the Ghost Fleet research program.

==Intergovernmental relations with prefectural and metropolitan governments==

The Ministry of Defense conducts national territorial defense through structured statutory coordination with the forty-eight prefectures and metropolises, principally [[Okami Metropolis]] and [[Toyozawa Metropolis|Toyozawa]], managing complex civil-military interfaces surrounding base host communities, air defense installations, and disaster relief mobilizations.

The ministry exercises regional liaison through eight Regional Defense Bureaus (地方防衛局 ''Chihō Bōei-kyoku''). Under Minister Yuriko Katsumata, the ministry fundamentally revised its approach to base-hosting prefectures, repudiating the unilateral operational directives common during previous conservative administrations. Addressing long-standing civilian grievances in base-heavy regions such as [[Ogasawara Prefecture]], [[Kagami Prefecture]], and [[Ishijima Prefecture]], Minister Katsumata enacted the Base Host Community Partnership Charter. This charter grants prefectural governors statutory veto power over the introduction of new unmanned offensive weapons systems, expands mandatory noise-abatement flight curfews, and establishes the Base Environmental Remediation Fund, which finances joint prefectural-military cleanups of perfluorinated compounds (PFAS) and heavy-water residues around naval and air facilities.

In civil protection and disaster mobilization, the ministry coordinates with Prefectural Crisis Management Bureaus under the Disaster Countermeasures Basic Act. Upon formal request from a prefectural governor, the Minister of Defense dispatches SDF units for disaster relief missions (災害派遣 ''Saigai Haken''). Under the 2026 Civil Defense Modernization Compact, the ministry pre-positioned modular engineering equipment, mobile water purification plants, and emergency satellite communication vehicles across all forty-eight prefectures and metropolises, ensuring that provincial emergency commanders can deploy military logistical support within two hours of a seismic or weather emergency without awaiting central bureaucratic clearance.

Relations with the [[Okami Metropolitan Government]] center on the defense of the national capital region, the protection of critical government infrastructure, and joint civil defense planning for the catastrophic Okami Bay Earthquake contingency. The ministry maintains continuous operational coordination with the Okami Metropolitan Disaster Management Bureau. Through the Joint Capital Defense and Resilience Forum, the ministry conducts semi-annual mass evacuation simulations, coordinates airspace defense protocols with metropolitan transport authorities, and maintains hardened underground emergency command bunkers linking the Defense Ministry headquarters in Ichigaya directly to the Okami Metropolitan Government Building in Shinjuku.

